    "owner for the purposes of compliance. For more information; https://brs.go.ke/wp-content/uploads/2023/03/MPSR-HANDBOOK-1.pdf WHAT IS LIQUIDATION OF COMPANIES? Liquidation is the process of winding up a business following an event of insolvency. Insolvency is defined as the inability of a company to pay its debts of one hundred thousand shillings (Kshs. 100,000) or more. Once a company is in liquidation, a liquidator is appointed to realize the company’s assets and make a distribution to credito",
