    "gestions from the industry players themselves. TOURISM Kenya is currently the third largest tourism economy in Sub-Saharan Africa after South Africa and Nigeria, according to the Ministry of Tourism and Wildlife. In a statement, the ministry said last year, travel and tourism grew by 5.6 per cent to contribute Sh790 billion and 1.1 million jobs to the Kenyan economy. This beats the average global growth of 3.9 per cent and the Sub-Saharan Africa average of 3.3 per cent. Kenya’s tourism performan",
