    "QUALITY ASSURANCE FREQUENTLY ASKED QUESTIONS [FAQs] 1. What are the marks of quality issued by Quality Assurance a) Standardization mark b) Diamond mark c) Fortification Mark 2. What is the Standardization Mark? The Standardization Mark is a product certification mark issued by KEBS under the Standards Act for products made in Kenya that demonstrate conformity to the relevant Standards or approved specifications. It is valid for 2 years and is renewable. It is also referred to as S-Mark or SM. 3",
    "specifications. It is valid for 2 years and is renewable. It is also referred to as S-Mark or SM. 3. Who issues the Standardization Mark? The Kenya Bureau of Standards issues the Standardization Mark on behalf of the Government of Kenya. 4. Who should apply for the Standardization Mark? Manufacturers operating in the Republic of Kenya. 5. What is the acquisition procedure? a) Access the KIMS portal through the link https://kims.kebs.org and sign up. Follow the application procedure as guided by",
