    "SPECIAL ISSUE Kenya Gazette Supplement No. 17 (Mombasa County Bills No. 11) REPUBLIC OF KENYA ––––––– KENYA GAZETTE SUPPLEMENT MOMBASA COUNTY BILLS, 2024 NAIROBI, 29th October, 2024 CONTENT Bill for Introduction into the County Assembly of Mombasa— PAGE The Mombasa County Finance Bill, 2024 .......................................................1 PRINTED AND PUBLISHED BY THE GOVERNMENT PRINTER, NAIROBI THE MOMBASA COUNTY FINANCE BILL, 2024 A Bill for AN ACT of the County Assembly of Mombasa to i",
    "IROBI THE MOMBASA COUNTY FINANCE BILL, 2024 A Bill for AN ACT of the County Assembly of Mombasa to impose fees, charges, levies, taxes and penalties enforceable by the County Government of Mombasa; to amend various county legislation related thereof and for matters incidental thereto ENACTED by the County Assembly of Mombasa, as follows— PART I —PRELIMINARY Short title and Commencement 1. (1) This Act may be cited as the Mombasa County Finance Act, 2024 and shall come into operation upon publica",
    "Act may be cited as the Mombasa County Finance Act, 2024 and shall come into operation upon publication in the Kenya Gazette. (2) The applicable fees, charges, levies, taxes and penalties under the Act shall be imposed with effect from 1st January, 2025. Interpretation 2. In this Act, unless the context otherwise requires— “authorized channel” means the channel through which persons to whom this Act is applicable shall effect payment to the County, including but not limited to a person appointe",
    "Act is applicable shall effect payment to the County, including but not limited to a person appointed as a County Revenue Collector by the County to collect revenue or any other mode of payment as may be prescribed by the County Government from time to time; “Business” means— (a) trade, commerce or manufacture, profession, vocation or occupation; (b) any other activity in the nature of trade, commerce or manufacture, profession, vocation or occupation; (c) any activity carried on by a person con",
    "erce or manufacture, profession, vocation or occupation; (c) any activity carried on by a person continuously or regularly, whether or not for gain or profit and which involves, in part or in whole, the supply of goods or services for consideration; “cess” means tax or fees chargeable on goods under section 7; “county executive committee member” means the county executive committee member for the time being responsible for matters relating to Finance; “County Government” means the County Governm",
    "time being responsible for matters relating to Finance; “County Government” means the County Government of Mombasa; “County public officer” means a county public officer within the meaning of section 2 of the County Governments Act, 2012; 2 The Mombasa County Finance Bill, 2024 “County Receiver of Revenue” mean the persons appointed pursuant to section 157 of the Public Finance Management Act, 2012; “County Revenue Collector” means the county public officer appointed pursuant to section 158 of t",
    "2; “County Revenue Collector” means the county public officer appointed pursuant to section 158 of the Public Finance Management Act, 2012 for the purpose of collecting revenue for the County Government and remitting it to the County Receiver of Revenue; “Defunct Local Authorities” means Municipal Council of Mombasa; and “Person” shall mean a natural or juristic person. PART II—TAXES, FEES AND CHARGES PAYABLE AND RATES APPLICABLE Taxes, Fees, and Charges 3. (1) The Taxes, Fees and Charges set ou",
    "RGES PAYABLE AND RATES APPLICABLE Taxes, Fees, and Charges 3. (1) The Taxes, Fees and Charges set out in the AMOUNT column of the schedule shall apply for the respective items listed in the “Particulars” column at the rate set out therein. (2) For greater certainty, the taxes, fees and charges applicable are payable to the County Government of Mombasa at the commencement of this Act. Transition 4. (1) All directions, resolutions, orders and authorizations on or relating to financial management,",
    "(1) All directions, resolutions, orders and authorizations on or relating to financial management, including the collection and administration of taxes, fees and charges given or issued by the Defunct Local Authorities and subsisting or valid immediately before the cessation of the application in the Local Government Act, Cap. 265 of Laws of Kenya (now repealed) shall be deemed to have been given, issued or made by or under the authority of the County Assembly until expiry, amendment or repeal",
    ", issued or made by or under the authority of the County Assembly until expiry, amendment or repeal of the direction, resolution, order, authorization on financial management shall continue with the necessary modification, apply both to the payment and administration of the taxes, fees, charges and other levies under this Act. (2) Subsection (1) does not apply to the specific respective amounts payable in respect of the taxes, fees, charges or other levies and, in that regard, the amount provide",
    "yable in respect of the taxes, fees, charges or other levies and, in that regard, the amount provided shall be applicable as provided for in the “Amount” column in the Schedule. (3) All directions, resolutions, orders, authorizations and provisions that are contained in the Rating Act cap 267, Mombasa County Revenue Administration Act, Mombasa County Tax Waiver Administration Act, Mombasa County Trade Licensing Act, Mombasa County Alcoholic Drinks Control Act, Public Finance Management Act, 2012",
    "rade Licensing Act, Mombasa County Alcoholic Drinks Control Act, Public Finance Management Act, 2012 and other related laws The Mombasa County Finance Bill, 2024 3 and subsidiary legislations that are concerned with revenue administration in the county shall be deemed to be part of this Act. Business Licence and Permit 5. (1) A person shall not carry out any business or service within the County without a valid licence or permit issued by the relevant County office. (2) A person who intends to c",
    "ithout a valid licence or permit issued by the relevant County office. (2) A person who intends to carry out any of the business listed in the schedule or the single business permit regulations shall apply for a licence or permit from any of the County offices or a designated agent as shall be prescribed by the County Government from time to time. (3) A person who applies for a licence or single business permit under subsection (2) shall be issued with a licence on the payment of the applicable",
    "usiness permit under subsection (2) shall be issued with a licence on the payment of the applicable fee, depending on the location and size of the business as specified in the schedule or the single business permit regulations. (4) A Licence or permit issued under subsection (3) must be visibly displayed at the business premise at all times. (5) A person who contravenes any of the provisions of this section commits an offence. Rent and Land Rates Applicable 6. (1) A person occupying any plot, st",
    "is section commits an offence. Rent and Land Rates Applicable 6. (1) A person occupying any plot, stall or house leased or rented out by the County Government shall pay rent or rates, whichever is applicable, at the rate specified in the Schedule. (2) A penalty of three percent per month shall be charged for any outstanding amount of rent or rates for a plot that remains unpaid for after the 31st day of March, every year. (3) A person who contravenes the provisions of subsections (1) may be evic",
    "day of March, every year. (3) A person who contravenes the provisions of subsections (1) may be evicted and shall be evicted if he or she fails to pay house rent for three consecutive months. (4) Registered religious institutions shall be exempted from payment of rent and rates. Market fees and Offloading charges 7. (1) Market fee shall be charged on the goods as specified in the Schedule. (2) A person who fails or hinders other person to pay the offloading charges or market fee set under the sc",
