    "s to pay the said fees, charges or licenses set under the schedule and the single business permit regulations commits an offence. Additional Fees, Tax, License, Offloading and Fees 9. (1) The County Executive Committee Member for Finance may amend any additional fees, tax, license, cess and fees schedules to supplement the current Schedule. (2) An amendment in subsection (1) shall be subject to approval by the County Assembly. PART III—PAYMENT Payment through an authorized channel 10. (1) A paym",
    "proval by the County Assembly. PART III—PAYMENT Payment through an authorized channel 10. (1) A payment to the County Government made under this Act shall be paid through an authorized channel which include, direct deposit through the county bank account and electronic Pay bill channel. (2) A County Revenue Collector authorized by the County Government to collect revenue shall have an identification card issued by the County Government which shall be worn visibly by such County Revenue Collector",
    "on card issued by the County Government which shall be worn visibly by such County Revenue Collector. (3) An official receipt shall be issued for a payment made to the County Government. (4) A person who makes a payment through an authorized channel shall demand an official receipt for such payment and every payment made through an authorized channel shall be evidenced by an official receipt. (5) A person shall not receive or collect any money on behalf of the County Government unless he or she",
    "A person shall not receive or collect any money on behalf of the County Government unless he or she has been appointed to do so or has authority as the receiver and collector of County Government Revenue. (6) A person who contravenes the provisions of this section commits an offence. Appointment of an Agent 11. (1) The County Executive Committee Member for Finance may by written notice addressed to a person— (a) appoint a person to be an agent of the County Government for the purpose of collecti",
    "o a person— (a) appoint a person to be an agent of the County Government for the purpose of collection or recovery of charges, permit fees, licence fees, rent, cess and such other fees, as may be necessary for carrying out the purposes of this Act; and (b) specify the amount of charges, permit fees, licence fees, rent, cess and such other fees to be collected or recovered by the agent. The Mombasa County Finance Bill, 2024 5 (2) An agent appointed under this section shall enforce and ensure comp",
    "County Finance Bill, 2024 5 (2) An agent appointed under this section shall enforce and ensure compliance with the provisions of this Act and shall remit all revenue collected to the County Government through the County Receiver of Revenue or as may be otherwise instructed in the appointment notice. (3) An agent unable to comply with subsection (2) shall within seven working days, notify the County Executive Committee Member for Finance in writing, setting out the reasons for his incapacity to",
    "ty Executive Committee Member for Finance in writing, setting out the reasons for his incapacity to comply. (4) The County Executive Committee Member for Finance shall accept the notification and cancel the appointment notice accordingly. (5) Unless a notification is given by an agent under subsection (3), moneys for the payment of charges, permit fees, licence fees, rent, cess and such other fees specified in the agent's appointment notice shall be presumed to be held by the agent and payable t",
    "specified in the agent's appointment notice shall be presumed to be held by the agent and payable to the County Government. (6) The County Executive Committee Member for Finance shall by notice in writing require a person to furnish him or her, within seven days from the date of service of the notice, with information showing any moneys which may be held by the agent for, or due by him to the County Government. (7) An agent who fails to pay money collected under this section within the time spe",
    "nty Government. (7) An agent who fails to pay money collected under this section within the time specified in the notice shall have the collection and recovery of that amount recovered as if it were tax due and payable by the agent and the due date of such payment shall be the date the amount should have been paid to the County Government. (8) An agent who makes a payment to the County Government under this section be deemed to have acted under the authority of the County Government and shall be",
    "under this section be deemed to have acted under the authority of the County Government and shall be indemnified in respect of that payment against all proceedings, civil or criminal, and all processes, judicial or extra-judicial, notwithstanding any provisions to the contrary in any written law, contract or agreement. (9) A person who wilfully makes any false or misleading statement, or wilfully conceals any material fact shall be guilty of an offence. PART IV—OFFENCES AND PENALTIES General Off",
    "conceals any material fact shall be guilty of an offence. PART IV—OFFENCES AND PENALTIES General Offences and Penalties 12. A person who commits an offence under this Act for which no penalty is provided shall be liable, on conviction, to a fine not exceeding two hundred thousand shillings or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding one year or to both. Offences by Staff of the County 13. A member of staff of the County Government or any other person having a duty to perform under this Act who—",
