    "SOURCE: Manual compilation - Supplier Credit Management for Kenyan SMEs KB: kb3_financing_credit THEME: Supplier Credit Management NOTE: Compiled from Kenya Bankers Association, CBK, and trade finance guidelines. July 2026. SUPPLIER CREDIT MANAGEMENT FOR KENYAN SMEs WHAT IS SUPPLIER CREDIT? Supplier credit (also called trade credit) is when a supplier gives you goods now and you pay later — typically in 7, 14, 30, or 60 days. This is one of the most common forms of business financing in Kenya, e",
    "lly in 7, 14, 30, or 60 days. This is one of the most common forms of business financing in Kenya, especially in retail and wholesale. Example: A mama mboga buys vegetables from a wholesaler worth KES 5,000 on Monday and pays when she sells them by Friday. This is supplier credit. 1. HOW TO GET SUPPLIER CREDIT IN KENYA Start small and build trust: Step 1: Pay cash for first 3-5 orders to establish reliability Step 2: Ask for 7-day credit on small order Step 3: Pay exactly on time — never late St",
    "reliability Step 2: Ask for 7-day credit on small order Step 3: Pay exactly on time — never late Step 4: Request 14-day credit after 3 months of on-time payment Step 5: Gradually extend to 30-day terms Key principle: Supplier credit depends entirely on your REPUTATION for paying on time Documents that help get supplier credit: - Business registration certificate (shows legitimacy) - Bank account statement (shows financial stability) - References from other suppliers you pay on time - KRA PIN (s",
    "statement (shows financial stability) - References from other suppliers you pay on time - KRA PIN (shows tax compliance) 2. LOCAL PURCHASE ORDERS (LPOs) An LPO is a formal written order from a buyer to a supplier promising to pay for goods or services. Banks can finance LPOs — giving you cash while waiting for payment. LPO Financing in Kenya: - Your bank advances up to 70-80% of LPO value - You receive goods, deliver to client, get paid, repay bank - Available at: KCB, Equity Bank, Co-op Bank, D",
    "ceive goods, deliver to client, get paid, repay bank - Available at: KCB, Equity Bank, Co-op Bank, DTB, NCBA - Requirements: Valid LPO from creditworthy buyer (government, large company) - Interest: 14-18% per annum - Processing time: 3-5 working days Government LPOs: - Most valuable for LPO financing - Register on Government Procurement Portal: supplier.treasury.go.ke - Government must pay within 30 days by law (AGPO regulations) 3. INVOICE FINANCING (FACTORING) Invoice financing lets you get p",
    "30 days by law (AGPO regulations) 3. INVOICE FINANCING (FACTORING) Invoice financing lets you get paid immediately for invoices that your customers will pay in 30-90 days. How it works: 1. You deliver goods/services and issue invoice to customer 2. You sell the invoice to a finance company (factor) 3. Factor pays you 70-85% immediately 4. When customer pays, factor sends remaining amount (minus fee) Factoring companies in Kenya: - Liquid Africa: liquidafrica.com - Pezesha: pezesha.com (digital",
    "ee) Factoring companies in Kenya: - Liquid Africa: liquidafrica.com - Pezesha: pezesha.com (digital platform) - NCBA Invoice Financing - KCB Invoice Discounting Cost: Typically 3-5% of invoice value Best for: Businesses with large corporate or government clients 4. MANAGING CUSTOMERS WHO OWE YOU MONEY (DEBTORS) Extending credit to customers creates debtor risk. Rules for extending credit to customers: - Always get customer details (ID number, phone, physical address) - Use written credit agreeme",
    "ers: - Always get customer details (ID number, phone, physical address) - Use written credit agreement (even simple form) - Set clear payment terms (7 days, 14 days, 30 days) - Maximum credit per customer: 10% of your monthly revenue - Never extend credit to more than 30% of your total customers Debt collection in Kenya: - First reminder: Phone call on due date - Second reminder: SMS + phone call 3 days after due date - Third reminder: Formal letter 7 days after due date - Legal action: Small Cl",
    "3 days after due date - Third reminder: Formal letter 7 days after due date - Legal action: Small Claims Court (claims up to KES 1,000,000) - File at: Small Claims Court, Milimani, Nairobi - Cost: KES 500 filing fee - Fast: Cases resolved within 60 days 5. PAYMENT TERMS NEGOTIATION When buying from suppliers: - Always negotiate payment terms — most suppliers expect it - Offer something in return: larger orders, prompt payment, referrals - Common terms in Kenya: 7 days (Net 7), 14 days (Net 14),",
    "larger orders, prompt payment, referrals - Common terms in Kenya: 7 days (Net 7), 14 days (Net 14), 30 days (Net 30) - Early payment discount: Ask for 2% discount if you pay within 7 days When selling to customers: - Offer small early payment discount (1-2%) to improve cash flow - Charge late payment penalty (1-2% per month) for overdue accounts - State all terms clearly in your invoice 6. SUPPLY CHAIN FINANCING IN KENYA Large companies (Unilever, Bidco, Safaricom) offer supply chain financing p",
    "CHAIN FINANCING IN KENYA Large companies (Unilever, Bidco, Safaricom) offer supply chain financing programmes for their suppliers and distributors. How to access: - Register as approved supplier/distributor of large company - Large company guarantees your payment to bank - Bank offers lower interest rates because risk is lower - Ask your large company buyer if they have supplier finance programme Examples: - Safaricom Supplier Programme - Kenya Airways Supplier Finance - EABL (East African Brewe",
    "Examples: - Safaricom Supplier Programme - Kenya Airways Supplier Finance - EABL (East African Breweries) Distributor Finance",
