    "ld aim at growing MSEs to medium sized businesses, corporations and manufacturing industries, knowledge sharing through seminars and extension officers, ENABLING and business learning labs to support monitoring growth and provide advisory to the government. ENVIRONMENT b) Work in collaboration with academic institutions and research organizations to conduct need assessment which will act as a guide in designing trainings. a) Targeted social protection and economic stimulation: As the economy is",
    "e in designing trainings. a) Targeted social protection and economic stimulation: As the economy is recovering from the crisis, majority of the MSEs scaled down their operations by more than two times while others did not return to business. 46 per cent of the MSEs had closed business for more than a year. A few cases who had aborted the telephone interview claimed that’s they converted to other temporary jobs like riding motorbikes “boda boda” which may not be sustainable in the future. Policie",
    "emporary jobs like riding motorbikes “boda boda” which may not be sustainable in the future. Policies should be geared towards 1) short term recovery of lost businesses targeting growth-oriented enterprises, allocation of resources towards performing business 2) revival of firms that had a sustainable growth and operations before COVID-19 3) avoiding the risk of supporting businesses that would only survive if support was being provided to them. FINANCING AND b) Multi-lingual financial literacy",
    "ly survive if support was being provided to them. FINANCING AND b) Multi-lingual financial literacy trainings for MSMEs would support business growth as majority of the businesses GOVERNMENT interviewed were micro businesses led by individuals who had attained either primary or secondary school education. 56 SUPPORT per cent of these MSEs had been in operations for the last 4-10 years. c) Embrace learning from other working systems like education loan, Older Persons Cash Transfer (OPCT) among ot",
    "learning from other working systems like education loan, Older Persons Cash Transfer (OPCT) among others to develop support mechanism based on a social protection fund or low interest loans with minimized requirements on collaterals. d) Advocate for innovative financing programmes to start-up businesses or accelerate business growth; Grants from family and relatives forms majority of start-up businesses followed by loans from different organizations or groups. 24 Recommendations 2/3 a) Mapping o",
    "nesses followed by loans from different organizations or groups. 24 Recommendations 2/3 a) Mapping of existing gaps in collaboration with all related organizations especially the KRA, Kenya National Innovation Agency (KeNIA) and the county governments among others to set a roadmap or agenda towards closing the gaps and attaining targeted goals. CAPACITY b) Digital transformation requires access to services like electricity and network to propel online trading. Electricity BUILDING and network co",
    "services like electricity and network to propel online trading. Electricity BUILDING and network coverage are highly concentrated in the densely populated regions along central, west, and coastal regions. Close to half of Kenyans have access to smartphones according to research done by multiple research organizations and agencies. These can be tapped to grow MSEs by for instance investing in the national digital infrastructure so as to expand public access to internet facilities. a) Trade fair",
    "national digital infrastructure so as to expand public access to internet facilities. a) Trade fair and exhibition; marketing opportunities through trade exhibition at grassroot levels should be explored to EFFECTIVE increase market opportunities. SUPPORT b) Target majority support; within the COVID-19 period, the GoK implemented a package of tax measures. Only 5% of the STRATEGIES MSEs had tax registration certificate implying that majority of the MSEs did not benefit with measures on tax by th",
    "gistration certificate implying that majority of the MSEs did not benefit with measures on tax by the GoK. Moreover, majority of the businesses that did not have any trade license did not receive any government support. 25 Recommendations 3/3 a) Learnings from success in issuance of county trading license/ business permit can be used to effect policies aimed at devolving taxation to county level which would help the government increase tax base at the same time visibility of business landscape b",
    "hich would help the government increase tax base at the same time visibility of business landscape b) Articulate messaging; MSEA and other key organizations have initiated discussions on formalizing MSEs aiming at expanding access to government services and support. These efforts require articulate messaging on its benefits to the businesses like access to the government tenders and direct support among others. FORMALIZATION c) Targeted behavioral interventions; behavioral science experiments ha",
    "among others. FORMALIZATION c) Targeted behavioral interventions; behavioral science experiments have contributed to success the health sector and awareness and most recently in promoting COVID-19 vaccine uptake. Such experiments can be designed to help understand hesitancy to formalization and devise behavioral interventions. d) Previous financial access studies have found out that 30% of households in Kenya exist in an informal group. Targeting groups such as informal savings groups, business",
    "olds in Kenya exist in an informal group. Targeting groups such as informal savings groups, business communities and such alike as a means of formalization would advance access of members and the formalization agenda. 26",
